# TypeScript

- `strict: true`. No `any`; use `unknown` and narrow. No non-null `!` unless the invariant is proven nearby.
- Derive types from schemas (`z.infer<typeof ZapSchema>`) instead of duplicating interfaces.
- Model variants with discriminated unions and exhaustive `switch` (`assertNever`).
- `readonly` for inputs and config; avoid mutating arguments.
- Prefer `type` for unions/aliases, `interface` for object contracts implemented by classes.
- Named exports only; no default exports (except where a framework requires them).
- Import order: node built-ins, external, workspace (`@workflow/shared`), relative.
- File names: `kebab-case.ts` with role suffix (`zap.service.ts`, `zap.repository.ts`, `zap-list.component.ts`).

```ts
// ❌ BAD
function handle(e: any) { return e.data.id; }

// ✅ GOOD
function handle(event: PullRequestOpenedEvent): number {
  return event.pullRequest.number;
}
```

## Errors
- Throw typed domain errors (`NotFoundError`, `ForbiddenError`, `ValidationError`) extending a base `AppError` with an HTTP status; never throw strings.
- Wrap third-party failures with context and `{ cause }`.
